<title>USA: Cognizant says board approves buyback plan.</title>
<headline>Cognizant says board approves buyback plan.</headline>
<dateline>WESTPORT, Conn. 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cognizant Corp said its board approved a stock buyback program of up to 8.5 million shares, or five percent, of the company's outstanding common stock over a two-year period.</p>
<p>Stock purchases are scheduled to begin immediately, the company said.</p>
<p>Cognizant has about 170 million shares of common stock outstanding, it said.  The company's shares were up 1/8 in early afternoon trading at 32-5/8.</p>
</text>
